{"term":"launch","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:e0238985b39cfaa225","definition":"To throw (a projectile such as a lance, dart or ball); to hurl; to propel with force.","example":"There they were met by four thousand Ha'apa'a warriors, who launched a volley of stones and spears[…]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["fling","hurl","bung","cast","chuck","chunk","cook","dash","dump","feck","fling","jerk","heave","hield","hoy","huck","hurl","hurtle","launch","lob","peck","peg","pick","pitch","precipitate","project","quoit","shy","slight","skew","sling","thrill","throw","toss","traject","warp","whang","whip","whop","wing","yeet"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["air-launch","autolaunch","failure to launch","hard-launch","launchable","launchee","launcher","launch forth","launchful","launch into","launch lunch","launch one's lunch","launchway","mislaunch","outlaunch","overlaunch","postlaunch","prelaunch","relaunch","soft-launch","unlaunch","unlaunched"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/launch#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2cafd762d7b7005856","definition":"To pierce with, or as with, a lance.","example":"And launch your hearts with lamentable wounds.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["lance","pierce"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["air-launch","autolaunch","failure to launch","hard-launch","launchable","launchee","launcher","launch forth","launchful","launch into","launch lunch","launch one's lunch","launchway","mislaunch","outlaunch","overlaunch","postlaunch","prelaunch","relaunch","soft-launch","unlaunch","unlaunched"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/launch#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ddbd096a51d8756471","definition":"To cause (a vesse